From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:33:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: CB1's SDR displays and BT.2020 colours

The Vulkan engine's SDR output takes every display CroqueMr's CB1 SDR
rendering offers (DVVK_SDR_POWER, DVVK_SDR_BLACK, DVVK_SDR_BT2020, a
white from 20 cd/m2; dvvk_sdr_flags says what a library takes), but
Kodi could only ask for the displays of 0.5.1's two settings. Viewers
coming from CB1 expect its Reference and Bright room displays, a custom
one for a projector, and its BT.2020 output.

Settings > Player > Dolby Vision gets SDR display: Brightness and gamma
(the default: SDR display brightness and SDR gamma, as before),
Reference (100 nits, a pure 2.4 power, black 0), Bright room (200
nits, 2.2, black 0) and Custom (White 20 to 500 nits, Gamma 1.8 to 2.8,
Black 0 to 5 nits). It sets DV_SDR_TARGET and DV_SDR_CUSTOM_*, from
which the adapter makes the engine's mode (SdrDisplay). HDR10, HDR10+
and HLG videos through the SDR output take the same display.

The setting is offered where the library takes CB1's targets. A display
the library does not take, or custom values out of range from
native-dv.env, leave the SDR output unavailable (SupportsSDROutput: the
fallback chooses as on a display without it, with one log line) rather
than make the picture for another display; the setting stays shown
while such a value is saved, so that it can be set back.

BT.2020 colours (off by default, DV_SDR_BT2020) asks for
DVVK_SDR_BT2020. The window grants it to an SDR output it begins only
where the library has the flag, the connector's Colorspace has
BT2020_RGB and the display's EDID lists BT.2020 RGB (CB1's terms), and
logs why not otherwise. The engine says of each picture whether it is
BT.2020, and the commit that shows it stages the matching Colorspace (a
change is a modeset for the kernel), so a picture and its signal never
disagree. Three refused BT.2020 commits make the rest of the video
BT.709 from the next picture, with a notification; where none was ever
taken, BT.2020 is not asked for again until Kodi restarts. The restore
after the video sets Colorspace to Default, as before. Player
information's Signal names BT.2020.

Strings 45146 to 45160. With the defaults the engine's mode and the
connector's properties are those of before.
